      "writtenOn": "2026-01-20T16:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, I see what\u0027s happened here. This example case made me think that I would have expected that\u0027s already supported, and I should have noticed breaking it, but it\u0027s actually not. In current Tint:\n\n```\nv.x \u003d 42; // This is allowed (you can swizzle assign a single element)\n//v.yx.x \u003d 42; // This fails with error: cannot assign to value of type u32\n```\n\nSo if this change is to truly be a no-op, maybe we could keep the `\u0026\u0026 !memory_view-\u003eIs\u003ccore::type::SwizzleView\u003e()`s here with a better comment, but I\u0027ll follow up with a CTS test to catch this and fix it as a bug separately?",
